<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Borgu</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Borgu is a region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-africa">West Africa</a> straddling the border of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-empire">Benin</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a>, home to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bariba">Bariba</a> people. Around 1535, after a defeat by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nupe-kingdom">Nupe</a>, the ruling dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oyo-empire">Oyo</a> spent roughly eighty years in exile in Borgu. Contact with Borgu's equestrian warriors during this period strengthened the cavalry tradition of the Oyo Empire.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/borgu.jpg" alt="Borgu" width="320" height="196" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was Rollebon at Dutch Wikipedia. (Original text: Wikipedia Commons en Rollebon) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Borgu.jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
